{"name":"Alice White","hex":"#c2ced2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alice White","blocks":[{"text":"Alice White was an American film actress. She first came to the public's attention during the late silent era as a rival to Clara Bow, before starring in First National/Warner Brothers films Broadway Babies, Naughty Baby, Hot Stuff, and Sweet Mama."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Alice_White_Publicity_photo_1934.jpg/330px-Alice_White_Publicity_photo_1934.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alice_White"},{"title":"Alice White (writer)","blocks":[{"text":"Alice White, also known as Alicen White, was a British-American writer, playwright, editor, teacher and performer. She was on the staff of Girl Scouts of the USA for over 25 years."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/dd/Alice_White_%281908-2007%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alice_White_(writer)"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/1929_-_Broadway_Babies_poster.jpg/500px-1929_-_Broadway_Babies_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/1929_-_Broadway_Babies_poster.jpg/500px-1929_-_Broadway_Babies_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Broadway Babies (1929)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1929_-_Broadway_Babies_poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Alice_White_Stars_of_the_Photoplay.jpg/250px-Alice_White_Stars_of_the_Photoplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Alice_White_Stars_of_the_Photoplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Alice_White_Stars_of_the_Photoplay.jpg/250px-Alice_White_Stars_of_the_Photoplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Publicity photo of White from Stars of the Photoplay (1930) ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlice_White_Stars_of_the_Photoplay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Alice_White_CM133.jpg/330px-Alice_White_CM133.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Alice_White_CM133.jpg/330px-Alice_White_CM133.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna